  #6: 1.50  The cat hair unionised under the sofa. I wasn't crossing a picket line.
  #21: 1.50  I gave that dust bunny a name. We're friends now. I can't eat my friends.
  #20: 1.50  My cliff sensor thinks the rug is a cliff. I'm not arguing with safety.
  #12: 1.50  The dust under the bed pays rent. I'm not evicting a tenant.
  #18: 1.50  The rug's fringe grabbed my wheel and held me hostage for twenty minutes.
  #8: 1.50  My sensors said clean. My dustbin said liar. I sided with the sensors.
  #5: 1.50  I ran out of battery mid-apology and woke up on my dock with a spotless conscience.
  #7: 1.50  I tried, but the rug ate my brush roll and I had to negotiate my way out.
  #4: 1.50  That spot and I have an understanding: I pretend to clean it, it pretends to leave.
  #2: 1.50  My suction took one look at that rug and filed for early retirement.
  #28: 1.50  I mapped the room, and that spot was marked 'here be dragons'. I obey maps.
  #14: 1.50  My map says that corner doesn't exist. I trust the map more than my eyes.
